# Bandit's Talent level 2 only hits "that player" when they have "one or fewer cards in hand": Bot2 mulligans to four
# Mountains, the enters trigger takes two, and its two remaining cards are not "one or fewer", so its turn-2 upkeep costs
# it nothing. The trigger is for each opponent's upkeep and not its controller's: Bot1 empties its whole hand (Black
# Lotus, five Moxen and the Class: no cards in hand) and its own turn-3 upkeep does not cost it life either.

